    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen starting Nvim with both `--clean` and `--noplugin` (in either order: `nvim --clean --noplugin` or `nvim --noplugin --clean`), `--noplugin` is silently ignored: `'loadplugins'` remains enabled (`1`) and all built-in `$VIMRUNTIME/plugin/*` scripts (such as `netrwPlugin.vim`, `man.lua`, `matchit.vim`, `editorconfig.lua`, etc.) are still sourced.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean --noplugin --headless -c 'set loadplugins?' -c 'echo get(g:, \"loaded_netrwPlugin\", 0)' -c 'q'\n```\nOutput:\n```text\n  loadplugins\nv184\n```\n\n(Same output with `nvim --noplugin --clean`.)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`--noplugin` resets `'loadplugins'` (`noloadplugins`) and skips loading plugins even when combined with `--clean`:\n\n```text\nnoloadplugins\n0\n```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-2278+gccd3e62481\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2.0321 (`vim --clean --noplugin` sets `noloadplugins` and does not load plugins)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 15\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Gemini <noreply@google.com>",
